From ab7b0f1497e24c506fc459a4602e15ce61b20c42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:16:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] auth: PathOps Dex-first sign-in with a local break-glass
 route

PathOps Decision 0059: in a PathOps Cell the Cell's Dex is the one
interactive sign-in of Forgejo, and Forgejo-local username/password
sign-in remains only as an unlinked recovery route that does not depend
on Dex.

[service] PATHOPS_LOGIN_SOURCE names the OAuth2 authentication source
(the login_source name, unique) that is the normal sign-in. When set:

- GET /user/login redirects to /user/oauth2/<source> (redirect_to is
  kept in its cookie, signed-in users are redirected as upstream); when
  the name is not an active OAuth2 source it answers 503 with the
  sign-in page without the local form, never falling back to it;
- POST /user/login is refused (403): local credentials are accepted
  only at the break-glass route;
- GET and POST /user/login/break-glass serve the upstream local sign-in
  form and handler (2FA, captcha, remember-me unchanged), without the
  OAuth2 sources, so nothing on the route reaches the provider. It is
  not linked from any page and exists only while ENABLE_INTERNAL_SIGNIN
  is true.

The OAuth2 sign-in and callback routes, auto-registration and account
linking are unchanged. Without the setting the routes and pages are
upstream's and /user/login/break-glass is 404.
